solution:
Use \(2^0=1\) and \(2^{-k}=1/2^k\) for positive integers \(k\). The resulting fractions have denominators dividing \(16\), so multiplying the numerator and denominator by \(16\) removes all the fractional terms without changing the quotient:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac{2^1+2^0+2^{-1}}{2^{-2}+2^{-3}+2^{-4}}
&=\frac{2+1+\frac12}{\frac14+\frac18+\frac1{16}}\\
&=\frac{32+16+8}{4+2+1}\\
&=\frac{56}{7}=8.
\end{aligned}
\]
The denominator is positive, so the divisions are valid. The value is \(8\), choice B.

